  "findings": [
    "Desktop ordinary opening misses 60 FPS in all three races, including the production offline package; fixed-step simulation keeps up and is not the immediate early-stage limiter.",
    "Hiding only the original ground returns near-60Hz pacing while keeping most decoration draws, and half pixel ratio also helps; the ground material is the first optimization target.",
    "The ground shader samples eight color layers and eight normal layers per fragment plus masks and reveal. Reducing either set in diagnostic runs improves pacing.",
    "Map props account for most draw calls and CPU render submission, but hiding only props does not restore stable 60.",
    "At DPR1, native, balanced and performance all render at pixel ratio1, limiting the existing quality control for this bottleneck."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Ablations are diagnostic visual degradations and are not proposed for shipping.",
    "No independent GPU timer or physical-device/high-refresh display timing was collected.",
    "Stage3 and stage6 are controlled reference scenes; natural no-input run ended in defeat during stage1, so stages2–6 need real-operation acceptance after optimization.",
    "Small sequential samples on one host vary; no precise percentage improvement is claimed."
  ],
